window.COURTSIDE_BIO="<p class=\"bio-lead\">Eric Hudson is a litigation partner at Arambula Terrazas PLLC whose practice centers on complex commercial, construction, and employment disputes.  He brings nearly two decades of experience to business conflicts, trials, arbitration, injunctions, and appeals.</p>\n<p>Eric serves as first-chair counsel in state and federal courts, arbitration, and administrative proceedings.  His commercial work includes contract and payment disputes, trade secrets, construction claims, and business governance.  He has secured arbitration awards for a general contractor and a device manufacturer, obtained a jury verdict for a property investment firm, and successfully defended a steel manufacturer while pursuing its counterclaims.  His injunction practice includes protecting assets from dissipation before trial.</p>\n<p>Before joining Arambula Terrazas, Eric served as Senior Special Counsel in the Texas Attorney General\u2019s Special Litigation Unit, handling constitutional and election litigation.  His appellate experience includes the Texas Supreme Court and Fifth Circuit, as well as amicus representation before the U.S. Supreme Court.</p>\n<p>Read his <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.atlawpllc.com/eric-hudson\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">firm biography and representative matters</a>.</p>\n<h3 class=\"bio-media-heading\">Constitutional and religious liberty work</h3>\n<p>Alongside his commercial practice, Eric represents individuals and institutions in disputes over religious exercise, equal treatment, and governmental authority.  That work includes education, land use, regulatory enforcement, and the freedom to carry out religious practices.  It is part of a broader practice serving clients whose rights, businesses, and institutions are at stake.</p>\n<details class=\"bio-media-coverage\"><summary>Selected religious liberty matters and media coverage</summary><p>Eric served as counsel of record for the Legal Insurrection Foundation in <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/24pdf/24-297_4f14.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Mahmoud v. Taylor</em></a>, a U.S. Supreme Court case about religious exercise in public schools.  He filed an <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/24/24-297/351644/20250310153952277_24-297%20Amicus%20Brief.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">amicus brief in support of the petitioners</a>.</p><p>In coverage of an education case, Eric told <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.texastribune.org/2026/07/17/texas-vouchers-islamic-private-schools-sam-westrop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Texas Tribune</a> and <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.propublica.org/article/islamic-private-schools-texas-vouchers-sam-westrop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ProPublica</a>, \u201cReligious liberty is not a temporary pass issued after a lawsuit.\u201d  His work on disputes involving state investigations and land use has also been covered by <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.keranews.org/news/2026-02-17/texas-ag-paxton-files-second-lawsuit-related-to-project-formerly-known-as-epic-city\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KERA News</a> and the <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/columnist/chris-tomlinson/article/republican-muslim-rhetoric-2026-election-22247861.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Houston Chronicle</a>.  <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.texasmonthly.com/news-politics/abbott-paxton-fraud-epic-mosque/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Texas Monthly\u2019s October investigation</a> examined the state\u2019s securities case.</p><p>Eric also represents the East Plano Islamic Center (EPIC) in its federal lawsuit against the Texas Funeral Service Commission, a case concerning the right to carry out religious funeral rites.  <a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.tpr.org/news/2026-06-29/theres-no-evidence-plano-mosque-applies-sharia-law-in-its-funeral-practices-a-federal-judge-says\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KERA News covered the case in an article republished by Texas Public Radio</a>.</p><details class=\"bio-media-coverage\"><summary>More media coverage</summary><ul><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://texasstandard.org/stories/texas-school-voucher-application-deadline-extension-islamic-muslim/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Texas Standard and Houston Public Media on the application deadline</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://news.bloomberglaw.com/litigation/texas-muslims-win-application-extension-in-school-choice-program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bloomberg Law on the federal court\u2019s extension</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.star-telegram.com/news/local/education/article315090933.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fort Worth Star-Telegram on the application window</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://baptistnews.com/article/faced-with-with-lawsuit-texas-admits-muslim-schools-to-voucher-program/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Baptist News Global on access to the education program</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.kwbu.org/news-from-across-texas/2026-04-23/texas-school-voucher-award-notices-sent-to-first-group-of-families\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Public radio coverage of voucher awards and the litigation</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.texastribune.org/2026/02/13/epic-hud-north-texas-islam-muslim-housing-development/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Texas Tribune on the federal housing investigation</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.keranews.org/news/2026-03-11/ag-paxton-urges-collin-county-to-deny-applications-for-muslim-housing-development\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KERA News on the land use dispute</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.keranews.org/news/2026-04-29/travis-county-court-says-texas-agency-must-comply-with-agreement-made-with-muslim-housing-community-epic-collin-county\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KERA News on the agreement with a state agency</a></li><li><a class=\"bio-media-link\" href=\"https://www.keranews.org/news/2026-05-01/texas-ag-ken-paxton-says-he-suspended-a-tro-in-muslim-developments-lawsuit-can-he-do-that\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KERA News on the dispute over a court order</a></li></ul></details></details>\n";